   "source": [
    "# 🐍 + 📊 + 🤖  Python · R · pi-coding-agent\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome! This Binder ships with **Python 3.11**, **R 4.4**, and the\n",
    "**[pi-coding-agent](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent)**\n",
    "preinstalled — everything you need for data exploration, modelling, and\n",
    "AI-assisted coding.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🔬 Python quick start\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a new notebook, select the **Python 3** kernel, and go:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np, pandas as pd, matplotlib.pyplot as plt, seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame({'x': np.linspace(0, 10, 50)})\n",
    "df['y'] = np.sin(df['x']) + np.random.randn(50) * 0.1\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.lineplot(data=df, x='x', y='y')\n",
    "plt.title('Hello from Python!')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📊 R quick start\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a new notebook, select the **R** kernel:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "library(ggplot2)\n",
    "\n",
    "df <- data.frame(x = seq(0, 10, length.out = 50))\n",
    "df$y <- sin(df$x) + rnorm(50, sd = 0.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ggplot(df, aes(x, y)) +\n",
    "  geom_line(colour = 'steelblue', size = 1) +\n",
    "  ggtitle('Hello from R!')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
